THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

ProxiMight depends on third-party components fetched at build time. Their
licenses are separate from the MIT license above and must be honored when you
redistribute a compiled ProxiMight binary:

  - Dear ImGui .......... MIT       (github.com/ocornut/imgui)
  - cimgui .............. MIT       (github.com/cimgui/cimgui)
  - GLFW ................ Zlib/libpng (github.com/glfw/glfw)
  - cJSON ............... MIT       (github.com/DaveGamble/cJSON)

Optional platform redirection drivers are NOT bundled and have their own
terms; ProxiMight only integrates against them at the user's discretion:

  - WinDivert ........... LGPLv3 / GPLv3 dual-license. Dynamically loading the
                          driver keeps your app's license separate, but READ IT
                          before you redistribute the .sys/.dll. See docs.
  - Wintun .............. Prebuilt driver under WireGuard's terms.
  - macOS NetworkExtension is an Apple system framework (no redistribution of
    Apple code); it requires an Apple-approved entitlement.

See docs/PRIVACY-SECURITY.md and docs/RESEARCH.md for the full picture.
